On the fourteenth day of my internship, I focused on input, 
output, pipes, and redirection in the Bash shell. I read the 
relevant sections from the Linux book and learned about 
standard input, standard output, and standard error.

I studied commands such as echo and printf and learned how 
output can be redirected to files using operators such as > and >>.
I also learned how the pipe operator | can be used to send the 
output of one command as the input of another command.

To support my learning, I continued studying The Missing 
Semester's Shell Tools and Scripting materials. I followed 
the examples and tried to understand how pipes and 
redirection can make command-line operations more efficient.
I also continued solving Bandit challenges and tried to 
use these concepts when they were useful.
